This repository was created for the purposes of CS193 and sets an introduction on how to use both git and github. 3. Staging, commiting, and pushing changes

After you have written your README.md that appears every time someone visits your repo, you should copy the following files inside your directory:

.bashrc

HISTCONTROL=ignoreboth      # skip duplicates and lines starting with a spaceshopt -s histappend         # add to the history file instead of overwriting it# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------HISTSIZE=10000              # commands remembered in this sessionHISTFILESIZE=20000          # commands saved to ~/.bash_history# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------# History# This line makes everything below apply only when a human is typing.[[ $- != *i* ]] && return# If this file prints anything in that situation, those programs break.# Programs like scp and rsync start a non-interactive bash behind the scenes.# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------# Stop here if this shell is not interactive.

.zshrc

    # the git branch, e.g.   user@host:~/cs240/hw1 (main)%    autoload -Uz vcs_info    precmd() { vcs_info }    zstyle ':vcs_info:git:*' formats ' (%b)'    setopt PROMPT_SUBST    PROMPT='%F{green}%n@%m%f:%F{blue}%~%f%F{yellow}${vcs_info_msg_0_}%f%# '    autoload -Uz compinit && compinit    # tab completionfi# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------# History# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------HISTFILE=~/.zsh_historyHISTSIZE=10000              # commands remembered in this session

.vimrc

set encoding=utf-8set backspace=indent,eol,start  " backspace works the way you expect" ---------------------------------------------------------------------------" ---------------------------------------------------------------------------set nocompatible            " use vim features, not strict old-vi behaviorsyntax on                   " color the codefiletype plugin indent on   " language-aware indentation (C, Python, ...)" To see what any option does, run inside vim:   :help 'number'" ---------------------------------------------------------------------------" Basics" ~/.vimrc — read by vim every time it starts." Lines starting with a double quote are comments."

.gdbinit

set history size 10000set history filename ~/.gdb_history# Print structs one field per line instead of one long line.set print pretty on# Don't ask "are you sure?" when you quit or restart a running program.set confirm off# Don't stop long output with "--Type <RET> for more--".set pagination off# ~/.gdbinit — read by gdb every time it starts.# Remember commands between gdb sessions (use the up arrow, like in bash).set history save on

.gitconfig

[color]    ui = auto# Aliases: `git st` runs `git status`, and so on.[pull]    rebase = true[core]    editor = vim# ~/.gitconfig: read by git every time it runs.[init]    defaultBranch = main

After adding all these files, we want a script that installs all our Runtime Components in their proper places

install.sh

#!/usr/bin/env bash## install.sh: put the rc files in this repository to work.## Usage:#   ./install.sh             install everything#   ./install.sh --dry-run   show what would happen, change nothing#   ./install.sh --no-omz    skip installing oh-my-zsh## What it does:#   1. Copies each rc file here into your home directory, e.g.#        ~/runtime_components/vimrc  ->  ~/.vimrc#      These are copies: after editing a file in the repo, run this#      script again to install the new version.#   2. Copies gitconfig to ~/.gitconfig.rc and tells git to also read it

We would like to be able to run the script directly. Execute chmod +x install.sh

Runs ls -al to ensure all the files are present

$ ls -altotal 44drwxr-xr-x 3 kameranis kameranis 4096 Sep 21 12:45 .drwxr-xr-x 4 kameranis kameranis 4096 Sep 21 08:19 ..-rw-r--r-- 1 kameranis kameranis 2823 Sep 21 08:29 .bashrc-rw-r--r-- 1 kameranis kameran
